      "content": "While recognizing the inevitability of the tech shift is crucial, framing UBI as the *only* logical conclusion is still a strong claim that essentialists might push back on based on alternative visions like just-transition tax credits. Critics will argue that market-driven universal basic income from \"robot taxes\" (or \"land value taxes\" as some prefer) is theoretically possible, making the policy choice one of political will rather than pure necessity. To maintain your argument's persuasiveness, you should acknowledge these economic alternatives (like the \"economic democracy\" models) while demonstrating why the current political system is uniquely ill-equipped to implement them compared to the standard UBI proposal.",
